  slug raw-own-tree-ascii-report-mandate
  base anima/.own + hive/.raw SSOT observability layer
  since 2026-04-28 (user directive: 'raw 추가 등록 => 사용자가 raw tree, own tree 등 요청시에 ASCII 형태로 리포트를 해주어야 한다. 스스로 강화정도, 연결 강화정도 등 등등 다양한 것들 표현 가능해야함. 육안으로 보고 개선 부분 파악가능하게')
  scope anima context — when user requests one of {'raw tree', 'own tree', 'tree report', 'tree 보여줘', 'raw 트리', 'own 트리', '트리 리포트'}, agent MUST produce ASCII tree visualization with strengthening + connection metrics + gap detection. Report substrate: tool/anima_raw_own_tree_report.hexa (canonical helper L3' lock candidate).
  rule tree-report MUST include ALL FIVE axes:
    (a) **hierarchy structure** — raw/own root → category buckets (routing-dispatch / meta-triad / proof-truth / uncategorized fallback) → individual entries
    (b) **strengthening level** — per-entry star tier (5-tier: ★★★★★ ≥20 / ★★★★ ≥12 / ★★★ ≥7 / ★★ ≥4 / ★ ≥1) computed from notes_count + follow_up_count + proof_count + why_count + deps_count
    (c) **connection strength** — outgoing deps count (cites-out) + incoming citation count (cited-by, computed across full corpus); refs[] list shows top-8 deps
    (d) **visual markers** — [*] live / [!] warn / [+] new / [-] deferred / [v] resolved (5 status states)
    (e) **gap detection** — per raw 95 triad-mandate; flag entries missing {slug, severity, proof, why, enforce-layer-rationale (when enforce-layer present)} fields
  enforcement when user requests 'raw tree' / 'own tree' / 'tree report' / equivalent Korean phrase, agent invokes `hexa run tool/anima_raw_own_tree_report.hexa --own-tree` (or --raw-tree / --combined / --strength-mode) → runs python3 helper → emits ASCII tree to stdout. Output MUST be visually scannable for 육안 개선부 파악 (visual gap-spotting for governance refinement).
  exception non-tree user queries (specific rule lookup / single-entry inspection) — direct grep/read response sufficient; full tree report is ONLY for explicit tree-mode requests.
  bans hand-rolled ad-hoc ASCII trees that bypass canonical helper (drift risk — strength tier formula must be consistent across sessions; raw 142 D2 try-and-revert mirror = single-source-of-truth for tree formatter).
  bans tree-report without gap-detection section (raw 95 triad-mandate visibility requirement — gaps MUST surface even when none detected, explicit 'GAPS: none' line)
  why anima own SSOT (12 entries) + hive raw SSOT (154 entries) growth (~165 active rules, ~5800 LoC combined) exceeds eyeball-scan threshold. Without structured ASCII visualization, governance refinement (which entry needs strengthening / which has weak connections / which violates raw 95 triad) requires manual grep-walk per entry → wallclock prohibitive + omission risk. Tree-report = 육안 단위 governance scan substrate. Strength + connection metrics make 'where to invest next' immediately visible. Gap detection enforces raw 95 triad-mandate as a passive surveillance layer (not blocking, but constantly visible).
